# `prettier --write .` walks the whole repo. This file is the allow-list in
# reverse: only files hand-written in this session may be reformatted. Anything
# pre-existing, generated, or frozen is listed below with the reason.

# --- Tooling output / lockfiles -------------------------------------------
# Machine-managed. Reformatting a lockfile churns the diff and can break the
# integrity hashes readers rely on.
node_modules/
dist/
packages/js/dist/
coverage/
.turbo/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Frozen data contract (D1) ---------------------------------------------
# The 72 JSON files under data/ are gated on byte-identity. Prettier would
# re-indent the 592 KB algeria.json and every by-wilaya/*.json, which is exactly
# the diff the byte-identity test exists to catch. The build script owns this
# directory's formatting, not Prettier.
data/

# --- Generated source -------------------------------------------------------
# Emitted by scripts/build-data.ts. Formatting is the emitter's responsibility;
# a Prettier reflow here would show up in review as what looks like a data
# change. Fix formatting in the emitter, never in the output.
packages/js/src/generated/

# --- Not ours ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal planning documents. Reformatting someone else's prose is noise.
docs/

# --- Pre-existing, must stay byte-identical ---------------------------------
# Everything below shipped before this session. The acceptance criteria require
# these files to be unchanged, so Prettier must not touch them. Listed
# individually rather than by directory glob so that new session-authored files
# (tests/, scripts/build-data.ts, packages/js/src/index.ts, types.ts) stay
# formatted.
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
RUNBOOK.md
LICENSE

schema/
.github/
packages/python/

packages/js/README.md

# --- Frozen v1 benchmark fixture ---------------------------------------------
# v1.0.0 source, unmodified except for the data path. Reformatting it would
# make the "before" column a paraphrase rather than a measurement.
benchmarks/v1/

# --- Generated exports -----------------------------------------------------
# exports/csv and exports/sql are emitted by scripts/build-data.ts and gated on
# byte-identity exactly like data/. Prettier has opinions about neither CSV nor
# SQL, but it would rewrite them if a plugin ever added some.
exports/
